description:
Intent i021 (peer-trusted-transport, snapshot s05) complete. One finding reported (medium confidence): drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c:833-838 (quote: "chunk_size = le32_to_cpu(hdr.chunk_size);
	left_size = le32_to_cpu(hdr.left_size);

	if (avail < sizeof(hdr) + chunk_size) {"). Untrusted source: the glink TX_DATA header is peeked from the shared-memory RX fifo to the remote QCOM subsystem; chunk_size/left_size are raw peer-written 32-bit fields. Missing local limit: the sole check compares chunk_size against glink_smem_rx_avail() (qcom_glink_smem.c:70-76), which is computed from the same peer-writable SMEM head/tail words (head = le32_to_cpu(*pipe->head)) - a validated-fetch/later-independent-fetch violation - and there is no clamp against pipe->native.length or any kernel-known maximum. Unsafe use: qcom_glink_rx_peak(glink, intent->data + intent->offset, sizeof(hdr), chunk_size) at qcom_glink_native.c:897-898 copies peer-length bytes into an intent buffer sized by a different peer field (kmalloc(chunk_size + left_size) at 859/867 in intentless mode, or the peer's own earlier INTENT announce via le32_to_cpu(msg->intents[i].size) at 972), with the unsigned space check at 890 comparing peer values; glink_smem_rx_peak's wraparound branch (qcom_glink_smem.c:95-96) then copies the remainder from fifo offset 0. Result: malicious remote-subsystem peer can drive OOB read/OOB write past the kmalloc'd intent buffer into rpmsg callbacks. Counterevidence checked: the 890 check bounds honest-intent writes, upstream assumes a cooperative peer, and no userspace exfil path was proven - reflected in medium confidence and limitations. Additional candidates classified: greybus es2.c:844 safe (HCI-bounded actual_length plus msize/buffer_size_max checks), greybus operation.c:1038 safe (no unbounded deliverer in s05), 9p trans_virtio.c:140 safe (msize-clamped, header equality check), virtio_net.c:944 safe (truesize/MAX_SKB_FRAGS checks), qcom_glink_native.c:942 safe (struct_size + avail check), nbd.c:713 safe (fixed header, kernel-issued tag cross-checks). Bounded negative evidence for the rest of s05: 9p trans_rdma/trans_xen, ceph/cifs/smb reply parsers, fuse, xen-blkfront/back, mctp, nfc NCI, vhost, and virtio_rpmsg_bus were enumerated but not deep-read; no runtime reproducer was built (read-only tree, requires QCOM SMEM peer). Final artifact: /mnt/raid/home/yangshuangning/vuln_variant_search/experiments/clairvoyant_variant_search/runs/10_cluster/C9/agent-state/findings/i021.json with snapshots_checked=["s05"], execution_status=complete.
